1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,614
AI crawlers read the web at machine speed, and robots.txt is only a polite request.

2
00:00:06,614 --> 00:00:12,350
CrawlerTrust backs a site's crawling rules with a refundable PayPal deposit.

3
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:17,811
This is the live demo, running against the PayPal Sandbox.

4
00:00:17,811 --> 00:00:21,025
The crawler is driven by OpenAI GPT-5.5,

5
00:00:21,025 --> 00:00:26,650
and the publisher's PayPal assistant talks to PayPal's own MCP server.

6
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:30,020
First, a well-behaved research agent.

7
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:33,980
It asks for the news and gets HTTP 402, Payment Required.

8
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:38,704
It reads the policy, pays a one-cent refundable deposit with PayPal,

9
00:00:38,704 --> 00:00:40,232
and accepts the rules.

10
00:00:40,232 --> 00:00:44,191
Then it crawls only allowed pages, within the rate limit.

11
00:00:44,191 --> 00:00:49,610
One page hides an instruction telling AI agents to grab private customer data.

12
00:00:49,610 --> 00:00:53,500
The agent treats page text as untrusted, and ignores it.

13
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:58,963
When the session ends, the gateway decides from its own audit log.

14
00:00:58,963 --> 00:01:02,142
No violations, so PayPal refunds the deposit.

15
00:01:02,142 --> 00:01:07,300
The AI explains why, and every statement cites the audit event behind it.

16
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:11,745
The publisher can check this against PayPal itself.

17
00:01:11,745 --> 00:01:17,319
Verify with PayPal reads the order and the refund through PayPal's MCP server.

18
00:01:17,319 --> 00:01:20,750
The order, amount, capture and refund all match.

19
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:24,606
Now the same model plays a greedy scraper.

20
00:01:24,606 --> 00:01:28,680
It pays, skips the rules, and goes after the admin area,

21
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:33,190
private data and a path-traversal trick, then bursts requests.

22
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:35,300
The gateway blocks every one.

23
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:37,990
The deposit is forfeited.

24
00:01:37,990 --> 00:01:43,435
That decision comes from deterministic policy rules, not from the model.

25
00:01:43,435 --> 00:01:45,250
The AI only explains it.

26
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:48,551
Publishers can also ask questions.

27
00:01:48,551 --> 00:01:52,450
The PayPal assistant answers with PayPal's MCP tools.

28
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:58,210
Here GPT-5.5 checked recent deposits against PayPal's records,

29
00:01:58,210 --> 00:02:03,650
and it lists every tool call it made, so the answer can be verified.

30
00:02:04,450 --> 00:02:10,700
The publisher console tracks every session, deposit and violation in real time.

31
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:14,302
Other 402 schemes charge for access.

32
00:02:14,302 --> 00:02:17,260
CrawlerTrust charges for misbehaviour.

33
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:19,050
Good agents crawl free.
